Framework v26 Phase 1 — Kubernetes Deployment Contract
Validation evidence recorded: 2026-11-01
Environment: Go 1.27.3 windows/amd64; Windows PowerShell. Initial Phase 1 worktree
was clean at a91cec785; follow-up continued from the committed Phase 1 artifacts.
No cache/temp environment overrides were applied.

Scope and acceptance
--------------------
Phase 1 is technically accepted and complete; Phase 2 is not authorized. The three
products are registry-backed planning scope, not user approval. Human review and
explicit runtime authorization remain Phase 2 prerequisites. No production charts,
bootstrap, framework probes, deployment, or cicd-workflow runtime changes were made.
No Docker/K3s runtime acceptance is claimed.

Registry and inventory evidence
-------------------------------
Registry: 7 PS-IDs, 3 products, 1 suite (no guessed fourth product).
Default full inventory: 55 releases; 147 pools; 294 active application pod identities;
63 PostgreSQL logical databases per node; 84 active SQLite PVC identities. Defaults
remain min=max=2. The `p:identity:mixed-disk` projection is 1 release / 10 pools /
20 pod identities / 5 databases. Expanded pod inventory is preflight-limited at
10,000 records and rejected before enumeration rather than silently clamped.

The same pure graph generates the exhaustive deployment tree and persistent expected
JSON. Exact-byte `-check` passed for both artifacts. Repeated tree and JSON generator
