The first direct named-file lint exposed duplicate literals, missing error wrapping/checks,
and a test whitespace issue; those were corrected before the final clean lint result.
Case-insensitive `encoding/json` struct-field matching was also reproduced and rejected
before decode, while dynamic override keys were kept exact.

Earlier transient and remaining limitations
--------------------------------------------
An initial normal/tagged build attempt could not download several modules through the
configured proxy. An unchanged retry succeeded; dependencies, proxy settings, and cache/
temp environment were not modified.

The first commit-hook run showed that the shared JSON formatter sorts keys and uses
two-space indentation, unlike the initial serializer. Canonical output now matches the
formatter and exact-byte parity passes.

Windows validation did not run mutation testing; no mutation score is claimed. No
Docker/K3s/Helm runtime validation was attempted or implied. Phase 2 remains unauthorized.
